<% content_for :title, "Acme Salary Management" %>

<main class="home">
  <header class="home__header">
    <p class="home__eyebrow">Acme HR</p>
    <h1>Salary Management System</h1>
    <p class="home__lead">
      One place for HR to keep employee salary records and salary history for about 10,000 employees
      across several countries, and to review salary analytics.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="features-heading">
    <h2 id="features-heading">What it does</h2>
    <ul class="home__cards">
      <li class="home__card">
        <h3>Employees</h3>
        <p>Add and update employees, then search, filter, and page through the directory.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="home__card">
        <h3>Salary history</h3>
        <p>Salaries have effective dates. A change starts a new period, and earlier periods are kept.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="home__card">
        <h3>Bulk corrections</h3>
        <p>Upload a CSV or Excel file to correct many salaries at once. Rows that fail can be downloaded, fixed, and uploaded again.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="home__card">
        <h3>Analytics and reports</h3>
        <p>Salary summaries, distributions, and breakdowns, shown per currency. Different currencies are never added together.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="home__access" aria-labelledby="access-heading">
    <h2 id="access-heading">Access</h2>
    <p>
      Sign in through the HR web application. Salary data is available only to the signed-in HR manager;
      this page shows none.
    </p>
    <p class="home__meta">
      API service status: <%= link_to "health check", api_v1_health_path %>
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="home__footer">
    <p>Development and demo environments use synthetic data only.</p>
  </footer>
</main>
